        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Paint Composition",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\n  CHEMISTRY:\n    Acrylic polymer: typically poly(methyl methacrylate) or\n    poly(butyl acrylate) or copolymers thereof\n    Emulsified in water as particles (~100-300 nm diameter)\n    Coalescence mechanism on drying (see 00-OVERVIEW.md)"
    },
    {
      "id": "02-PAINT-COMPOSITION.md#010",
      "path": [
        "02-PAINT-COMPOSITION.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:coatings:02-paint-composition, git-history:coatings:02-paint-composition]",
        "canonical_path": "coatings/02-PAINT-COMPOSITION.md",
        "concepts": "[paint, composition]",
        "current_path": "coatings/02-PAINT-COMPOSITION.md",
        "id": "maxim:coatings:paint-composition",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "coatings",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[paint, composition]",
        "section": "coatings",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Paint Composition",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "\"100% ACRYLIC\" vs \"VINYL-ACRYLIC\":\n    100% acrylic: all-acrylic emulsion binder\n      → better UV stability, adhesion, flexibility, durability\n      → required for quality exterior coatings\n    Vinyl-acrylic (VAE): vinyl acetate copolymerized with acrylic\n      → cheaper; adequate for interior; inferior for exterior\n      → watch for in budget brands"
    },
    {
      "id": "02-PAINT-COMPOSITION.md#011",
      "path": [
        "02-PAINT-COMPOSITION.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:coatings:02-paint-composition, git-history:coatings:02-paint-composition]",
        "canonical_path": "coatings/02-PAINT-COMPOSITION.md",
        "concepts": "[paint, composition]",
        "current_path": "coatings/02-PAINT-COMPOSITION.md",
        "id": "maxim:coatings:paint-composition",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "coatings",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[paint, composition]",
        "section": "coatings",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Paint Composition",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "KEY PROPERTIES:\n    MFFT (minimum film formation temperature): ~40-50°F for most latex\n    Application below MFFT: chalky, non-coalesced, powdery film\n    Dry time: 1-2 hours (vs 6-8 for alkyd)\n    Recoat: 4 hours (dry to recoat) vs 16-24 hours (alkyd)\n    Full cure: 2-4 weeks for maximum hardness and washability"
    },
    {
      "id": "02-PAINT-COMPOSITION.md#012",
      "path": [
        "02-PAINT-COMPOSITION.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:coatings:02-paint-composition, git-history:coatings:02-paint-composition]",
        "canonical_path": "coatings/02-PAINT-COMPOSITION.md",
        "concepts": "[paint, composition]",
        "current_path": "coatings/02-PAINT-COMPOSITION.md",
        "id": "maxim:coatings:paint-composition",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "coatings",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[paint, composition]",
        "section": "coatings",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Paint Composition",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "WATERBORNE ALKYD (hybrid):\n    Alkyd resin emulsified in water\n    Better leveling and penetration than straight latex\n    Slower dry than latex, faster than oil alkyd\n    Used for: premium trim paints marketed as \"oil quality, water cleanup\"\n    Examples: Benjamin Moore Advance, Sherwin-Williams Emerald Urethane\n```"
    },
    {
