        "section": "coatings",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Paint Composition",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "PROPERTIES:\n    Superior leveling (self-levels from brush marks): smooth finish\n    Better cold weather application (vs latex that fails to coalesce)\n    Excellent adhesion to chalky surfaces, bare wood, old oil paint\n    Yellows (especially in dark areas): oxygen-deprived areas don't cure\n    Long dry time: 6-8 hours touch dry; 16-24 hours recoat\n    Full cure: 30 days\n    Solvent: mineral spirits → VOC; cleanup requires solvents"
    },
    {
      "id": "02-PAINT-COMPOSITION.md#017",
      "path": [
        "02-PAINT-COMPOSITION.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
